#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I start &krdc;, I get a message box that reads <computeroutput> "
"Browsing the network is not possible. You probably did not install SLP support "
"correctly.</computeroutput> What is wrong?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"SLP is Service Location Protocol, and is typically provided by <application>"
"OpenSLP</application>, or by <application>The Knot</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you compiled &krdc; yourself, this probably means that &krdc; has been "
"compiled against the SLP libraries, but the server (probably called <command>"
"slpd</command> or <command>knotd</command>) isn't running. You normally need to "
"start these servers as the superuser, which may mean requesting that your "
"system administrator does this, if you can't do this yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are running a packaged version of &krdc;, then you may have some missing "
"dependencies. There are so many ways this can happen that you'd need to seek "
"support from whoever did the packaging."
msgstr ""

